shirudo: Claude's working notes
===============================

This is a short cross-session scratchpad. Trust the code and git log
over stale notes; keep the implementation and this file aligned.

CURRENT STATE
-------------

The implemented MVP includes init, target-local status, keys, upatch
build/load/unload/list/info/get/map, TPM measurement, eventlog,
structured reports, the BPF enforcement hooks, and the systemd reboot
unit. The operator builds and signs artifacts; existing scp/ssh is used
to transfer and invoke target-local commands.

The former operator-side nodes, rollout, remote registry, selector, and
SSH transport paths have been removed. The target no longer collects status or
accepts rollout requests from shirudo. `shirudo status` is local-only.

Tests include the operator/build suite, target VM integration suite,
and the command-surface regression test that verifies the removed
top-level commands are rejected.

REMAINING WORK
--------------

Deferred by design: initramfs-stage init, atomic LSM updates, upgrade
workflow, TPM attestation, HSM-backed signing, audit ringbuf draining,
certificate rotation/revocation, and eventlog rotation.

Kernel-blocked work is tracked in TODO.kernel. Residual security
limits are documented in Documentation/threat-model.rst.
